      "text": "**Possibly somewhat, but don’t count on clear air tomorrow, Sunday, October 18.** Singapore’s National Environment Agency expects showers and a wind shift that *could* reduce smoke arriving from Kalimantan. It also warns that smoke from Sumatra may still drift toward Singapore. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nI couldn’t find an official PSI forecast specifically for October 18 yet—the **150–230** forecast you may see is for **October 17**, not tomorrow. Check NEA’s updated forecast before making outdoor plans, and its **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading** before heading out. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))",
